        "id": 49212,
        "name": "jagarciao",
        "username": "jagarciao",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/{size}/2010_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-12-10T20:38:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree it doesn't really matter THAT much. &nbsp;In fact I think the idea of having some heroes be \"weaker\" than others helps the game have different levels... as long as they are all fun to play. So if you dominate the game with one hero you might want to try doing so with a hero that is considered weaker.&nbsp;</p><p>I don't think there needs to be an official ranking of heroes since that will just create a million threads saying how this ranking or that rankin is wrong. Within a few games you figure out which heroes give you what type of experience and you cater your game to that. Also, more experienced players can use the \"weaker\" heroes when playing alongside new players to give the team a more balanced fee, etcetera. I know there has been discussion ad nauseum regarding some heroes being too weak compared to others... and I think there is some merit to that, but taking down a strong villain with a team of weaker heroes feels so very satisfying, and to me, that makes it all worth it.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:22:36.719Z",
