        "created_at": "2012-12-11T03:25:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jagarciao\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/48/2010_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jagarciao:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>IIn fact I think the idea of having some heroes be \"weaker\" than others helps the game have different levels… as long as they are all fun to play.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>My thought exactly. How awesome is it to defeat an interstellar warlord with guns and a broom? &nbsp;If people are frustrated more often then not when playing a character, that's more damaging for a first time player than power level.</p>",
